{"text":"Based on the provided context and multiple readings, the deviation of the UPPER_FLANGE has been confirmed to exceed the 2.0 micron tolerance threshold at various points, specifically at 2.1 microns and 2.5 microns. Given these out-of-tolerance readings, the CNC repair procedure is as follows:\n\n### Measured Deviation:\n- **UPPER_FLANGE**: 2.1 microns and 2.5 microns (both above the 2.0 micron tolerance threshold)\n\n### CNC Repair Procedure for UPPER_FLANGE:\n1. **Initialize the CNC Machine**:\n   - Power on the CNC machine.\n   - Load the part securely into the machining fixture.\n\n2. **Set Machine Parameters**:\n   - Set the spindle speed to 5000 RPM.\n   - Set the feed rate to 200 mm/min.\n\n3. **Execute Precision Milling**:\n   - Use a 1mm diameter end mill for fine adjustments.\n   - Perform precision milling on the UPPER_FLANGE area.\n   - Conduct multiple passes if necessary to achieve the required tolerance.\n\n4. **Post-Machining Inspection**:\n   - Inspect the machined part to ensure it complies with the 2.0 micron tolerance.\n   - Use metrology tools to verify the deviation is within the acceptable range.\n\n5. **Record Machining Data**:\n   - Save the machining data for quality assurance records.\n\nThis procedure should be followed to bring the UPPER_FLANGE back within the specified tolerance.","sessionId":"608d3c91-c04c-41b8-ae07-3ecf91d3ac9e-1","stopReason":"end_turn"}